    "question": {
      ":question/id": "edba6c94-17d8-580d-88d9-2631e9962256",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
